# Binding: your model, on your machine (a template)

Copy this file to `samples/binding.us` (which git ignores) and fill it in. A binding is
runtime config: the one place a model, its server and your machine are named. No profile, task,
board or eval set names a model.

- `api`: `ollama`, or `openai-compatible` for any other local server (llama.cpp's server,
  LM Studio, vLLM and the like). For `openai-compatible`, `endpoint` is the base URL that ends
  in `/v1`.
- `model`: the model as your server names it. Start with the smallest model that does tool calls.
- `provides`: what that model offers. A profile runs only on a binding that meets its
  `requires`; the samples need `tool_calling` and a 4096-token window.
- `hardware`: your machine, in words. Eval results are recorded against it.

If your server asks for a key, put it in the `STEW_API_KEY` environment variable yourself. It
never goes in a binding.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "binding",
  "name": "my-local-model",
  "api": "ollama",
  "endpoint": "http://127.0.0.1:11434",
  "model": "<your model's name>",
  "provides": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "context": 8192,
    "structured_output": false,
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "hardware": "<your machine, in words>"
}
```
